Consider $\triangle P Q R$ ．$T$ is a point on $P Q$ such that $P T: T Q=1: 2$ and $S$ is a point on $P R$ such that $P S: S R=(1-t): t$ ，where $0<t<1$ ．It is given that $Q, T, R$ and $S$ are concyclic．Let $\overrightarrow{O P}=\mathbf{i}+2 \mathbf{j}+2 \mathbf{k}, \overrightarrow{O Q}=25 \mathbf{i}+17 \mathbf{j}+5 \mathbf{k}$ and $\overrightarrow{O R}=-9 \mathbf{i}+37 \mathbf{j}-3 \mathbf{k}$ ，where $O$ is the origin．
\begin{itemize}
