Denote the origin by $O$ ．Consider $\triangle O P Q . A, B$ and $C$ are points lying on $O P, P Q$ and $O Q$ respectively such that $P A: A O=O C: C Q=Q B: B P=1: 2$ ．Suppose $A C$ and $O B$ intersect at a point $R$ ．
